sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (MorphoEval Loop 053 Assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Metzger et al. (2008) & Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mouse lung stereotyped branching modes (Domain D, Planar P, Orthogonal O) and FGF10-SHH-Ptch1 Turing mode selection — MorphoEval overall 47.0/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 1 (v1 baseline) evaluation of `2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py` (50.3/100). The v1 script sketches isolated geometric stick trees for Domain Branching (D), Planar Bifurcation (P, Delta_phi = 0 deg), and Orthogonal Bifurcation (O, Delta_phi = 90 deg), but omits compound lobar lineage grammars (e.g. Left Lobe D -> P -> O and D -> O -> O subroutines across E11-E15), omits the Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mesenchymal FGF10 + epithelial SHH/Ptch1 receptor-ligand reaction-diffusion PDE and dispersion relation that biochemically select between lateral domain budding and apical tip splitting, neither loads nor verifies `datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_reference.json`, and performs zero image segmentation on `bronchial_tree_specimen.jpg`. Overall 47.0/100 (faithfulness 40.3, reproducibility 62.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 58, Morphological realism / specimen match 20, Parameter expressivity 44, Morphometric validation 48, Source and data traceability 58, Code-to-model traceability 60, Reproducibility package 68. Output judged: docs/media/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_comparison.png: rendered output of 2008-metzger-lung-stereotyped-branching.py at 8871db0, image/png, 70750 B, 1755×598 px, artifact_sha256 f14f228fea1e4fad288bb3590cb0a837ad2d33ee635a6fb912eff070eead9277 (sha256 f14f228fea1e4fad288bb3590cb0a837ad2d33ee635a6fb912eff070eead9277), spec_fingerprint 253a37a14bc1e93edeec7f1a1f8bb0a117cab5067487066a4dceb4dff88210cb. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 253a37a14bc1e93edeec7f1a1f8bb0a117cab5067487066a4dceb4dff88210cb; artifact_sha256: f14f228fea1e4fad288bb3590cb0a837ad2d33ee635a6fb912eff070eead9277; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/bronchial_tree_specimen.jpg=3247bc8c35eddcad..., datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_reference.json=0a40515eda235917...}." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Expand `--self-test`, CLI parameter flags (`--mode-seq`, `--dihedral-deg`, `--bif-angle-deg`, `--domain-angle-deg`, `--a-f`, `--d-ratio`, `--generations`, `--seed`), and `measure_morphoeval()` to report >= 8 quantitative metrics with reference values, dispersion stats, and ablation deltas.",
            "remediation needed: Implement Metzger et al.'s (2008) full compound 3D lobar branching grammar combining Domain Branching (D_m along parent bronchus with 90 deg circumferential domain shifts) followed by Planar (P, Delta_phi = 0 deg at lobar margins) and Orthogonal (O, Delta_phi = 90 deg in lobar interior) subroutines, plus a randomized-dihedral negative-control ablation showing 3D self-collision / packing loss.",
            "remediation needed: Implement the Menshykau et al. (2012, 2014) mesenchymal FGF10 (F) + epithelial SHH/Ptch1 receptor-ligand (R) Schnakenberg-type reaction-diffusion PDE system and dispersion relation lambda(k^2), demonstrating the biochemical mode switch between apical tip bifurcation (P/O at low elongation speed) and lateral domain budding (D at high elongation speed).",
            "remediation needed: Load and SHA-256-verify `datasets/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes/lung_stereotyped_branching_modes_reference.json` and `bronchial_tree_specimen.jpg` at runtime, segment the mammalian bronchial tree specimen (extracting the smooth-muscle airway trunk, lateral domain branches, and terminal alveolar sac clusters, plus skeleton branch junction angles and inter-branch spacing), and validate against empirical E11-E15 mouse lung lineage benchmarks." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.47"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .
}

